  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency food and nutrition support to IDPs in hard-to-reach locations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As part of CAFOD&#x2019;s strategy to scale up its humanitarian response to reach out to people in hard-to-reach locations, the response through the informal ERRs/CBOs and faith structures on the ground in these locations has proved to be the easiest way to get aid to the people in hard-to-reach areas, in Sudan. Therefore, the project aims to reach 6000 families displaced and living on church premises and those frequenting the church premises to seek aid and support. The project will be delivered through Caritas Sudan, which in turn will work with 12 identified parishes in Khartoum, North Kordofan, South Kordofan, Blue Nile, North Darfur, River Nile, Gedaref, and Kassala, to provide the IDPs with food items. The support will also consider other immediate needs as may be identified by the parish leadership, dependent on available resources.</narrative>
  </description>
